Z||000004||loafer87gt||04-19-2000||03:18 PM||||The head mechanic at the dealership called today and said that I might as well come and pick it up from them because they have given up on the car. What a load of utter BULLSH*T! After charging me $1300 for parts and labor that didn't fix the problem, the tow bills, and being three weeks without the car they just give up. You guys have no idea how frustrated I am. This is the only dealership that was willing to work on my car, so I guess my only other option is to haul the car 300 kilometers to my old backyard mechanic. The problem if you guys didn't see in the tech section is that the car is stumbling and stalling, the revs surge from 1000 rpm to wherever position you have the throttle depressed to. So when you have the pedal down the car goes Blat-stall-blat-stall-blat! If you drive the car for 15 minutes and shut it off, and fire it back up it does this. This really sucks, its 20+ outside today and everyone is ripping around in their sportscars and I'm still stuck on my bike, it just ain't fair.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lennyb4||04-19-2000||03:26 PM||||Hey i cant blame you for being upset. But i have to agree with GT Bastard. Dont give up chief. Even if you do...why lower yourself to ricer status. When i first got my fiero it took me almost two months (and around $700) to get it just running, then i saw the light from above or could have been below (which led me here) and from reading all the post and asking questions my duck runs like a champ. I still have ALOT of resto work to do but i know with the help of all my new found friends it shouldnt be a problem...Thanks Guys.||||reg||1
